WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome to "Late Night."

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.968
We are gonna move on after this,
I promise,

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:07.267
and try our very best
to have a normal show,

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.234
but something happened
this weekend,

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:12.801
and we're gonna do our best
to address it now,

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.701
while appreciating
that we might not be

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:16.701
the best people
to talk about it.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:19.601
But on Saturday,
a gunman entered a supermarket

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.234
in a Black neighborhood
in Buffalo

00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:23.100
with an assault weapon
and shot 13 people,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.367
killing 10 of them.

00:00:24.367 --> 00:00:26.133
It's an absolute nightmare.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.734
And worse, it's a story

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:31.534
we've now seen
dozens and dozens of times.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:34.868
And this time,
there was a small detail

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:36.868
in the reporting
from The New York Times

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:38.601
that caught my eye --
just this one sentence.

00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:41.501
"A gun dealer who said
he sold the suspect

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:43.567
an assault weapon
in recent months

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:46.467
described
a routine transaction."

00:00:46.467 --> 00:00:48.133
We live in a country --

00:00:48.133 --> 00:00:49.501
and I don't know
when it happened --

00:00:49.501 --> 00:00:52.868
where an 18-year-old boy
goes into a gun dealership

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.234
to buy an assault weapon,
and it's a routine transaction.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:59.534
Under the same legal system
that won't let a person

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.434
buy a six-pack of Bud Light
because it would be dangerous.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:05.634
But an assault rifle,
that's routine now.

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:07.834
The implications is
that 18-year-old boys

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:11.801
go into that gun dealer and
buy weapons of war regularly.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:14.734
When a cable-news host
opens his show

00:01:14.734 --> 00:01:17.300
with a red-faced rant about
white people being replaced,

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.868
that's considered a typical
episode of that show.

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.901
Routine and typical.

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:25.567
Words like
"shocking" and "stunning"

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.133
are slowly draining out of
the conversation

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:30.167
about mass shootings,
and words like "routine"

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.901
and "typical"
are taking their place.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:34.267
I don't know what this means,

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:37.234
but it feels like bad news
on top of all the bad news.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.033
The usual voices are on TV today

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.667
blaming the dark corners
of the Internet,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.667
video games, and
offering thoughts and prayers.

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:47.534
And that, for sure,
is routine and typical.

00:01:47.534 --> 00:01:50.467
People are saying,
"We should concern ourself

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.968
with mental-health issues,

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:53.300
rather than
gun control or motive."

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.067
And maybe that's true
in some cases,

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:57.968
but in this case, the
motive was crystal clear.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:02:00.067
This shooter is
a white supremacist.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:02.868
And I'm sad
that hearing that phrase,

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:04.767
"The shooter is
a white supremacist,"

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.968
has also become routine.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:09.968
Incredibly sad.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:13.567
Now, those are just my thoughts
on these events,

00:02:13.567 --> 00:02:15.734
but this news
hit everyone differently.

00:02:15.734 --> 00:02:18.801
So, here with her own response
is one of our own writers,

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.367
Amber Ruffin.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.667
[ Applause ]

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.868
-Hey. Hey, everyone.
Seth is right.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:29.367
The news is awful.
I feel like [Bleep].

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:32.901
I feel unsafe.
This is an extremely bad day.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:37.767
But a bad day for me might
just be a good day for you.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:40.567
-How so, Amber?
-Let me show you.

00:02:40.567 --> 00:02:41.868
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:45.467
♪ Yes it's a good day for you,
not for me ♪

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:48.901
♪ And it's a good day
for sailin' at sea ♪

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.667
♪ Yes, it's a good day
'cause none of us are free ♪

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:56.467
♪ Till it's a good day for you
to denounce white supremacy ♪

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.334
-I'm sorry. What?
-I don't know, man.

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:01.067
I tried everything else.
Maybe a little song will do it?

00:03:01.067 --> 00:03:03.267
-Oh, Amber, you think a song
will change all this?

00:03:03.267 --> 00:03:06.100
-Dude, if this had been
the original words

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:10.100
to this old-ass song,
we may not be in this mess.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.934
-Amber!
-Oh, my bad.

00:03:11.934 --> 00:03:14.100
Let's try 400 more
"Closer Looks."

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.000
-Alright. Fair. Continue.
-Thank you.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.834
[ Up-tempo music continues ]

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:21.501
♪ And it's a good day
for taking a nap ♪

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:25.000
♪ And it's a good day
to dust off your cap ♪

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.767
♪ So pay attention
and avoid all the traps ♪

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.267
♪ Yes, it's a good day ♪

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:32.234
♪ To tell
your old racist relatives ♪

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:34.234
♪ You're not having
their crap ♪

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:35.667
-Amber?

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:38.000
-Someone has to try
to get through to them.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.901
I mean, have your attempts
been successful?

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.601
-Please continue.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.868
♪♪

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:48.567
-♪ I said to the sun,
good morning, sun ♪

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.868
♪ It's time to illuminate ♪

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:55.667
♪ And he said to me,
"Well, there's got to be ♪

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:58.901
♪ A way that we can get rid of
all of this hate ♪

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:02.667
♪ 'Cause it's a good day
to get a checkup ♪

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:06.300
♪ And it's a good day
to fill up your cup ♪

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.000
♪ So take a deep breath,
give your life a cleanup ♪

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.167
♪ 'Cause it's a good day
to realize ♪

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.300
♪ That these white supremacists
feel safe ♪

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:15.868
♪ In this society we created ♪

00:04:15.868 --> 00:04:18.267
♪ So it's the society
that has to change ♪

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.567
♪ And make these people
uncomfortable ♪

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:20.834
♪ And a good way
to start that is ♪

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.534
♪ When you hear them
say a racist thing ♪

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:23.634
♪ To tell them to ♪

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:26.367
♪ Shut ♪

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:27.534
♪ The ♪

00:04:27.534 --> 00:04:29.067
♪ [Bleep] ♪

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:32.834
♪ U-U-Up ♪

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:34.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:37.968
-Amber Ruffin, everybody!
Thank you, Amber.

